{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 52, "timestamp": 1790460158, "title": "node-triage: Claude Code triaging Slurm and Kubernetes over MCP", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/bash"}}
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[1mnode-triage demo\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mClaude Code + a Go MCP server over a real Slurm cluster and a Kubernetes cluster\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[2mClaude has only the node-triage tools: no shell, no files. SKILL.md is its playbook.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[1m1. Two failures at once\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[2m   classic Slurm: a GPU falls off the bus on slurm-c1 (slurmd now finds 3 of 4)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
